      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2017-11-21T17:59:44.563Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "59ea67485d6b1c6962d45a28",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "Having to press confirm every time you enter a portal is pretty jarring. We actually tried this before launch and all of us hated it. Having that be a toggle in the system menu hides it from most people so the entire VRChat travel experience gets clunky. We talked through the design of having to USE a portal and that had issues too including if it was a toggle in the system menu. There were some other good ideas but the one that won out for the moment is not being able to back into or go sideways through a portal. Including short back and forward movements. We've also added the name of the user who spawned the portal to help call out those spawning them in a troll like manner.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
